### Description

When calling a method with optional parameters we can use [`Type.Missing`](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.type.missing?view=net-6.0#remarks) as a place holder.
This works for most case, except for Nullable enum types.


### Reproduction Steps

```csharp
public static class DefaultParameter
{
    public enum YesNo
    {
        No = 0,
        Yes = 1,
    }

    public static void ShowEnum(YesNo? yesNo = YesNo.No)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"The value of the 'integer' parameter is: {yesNo}");
    }

    public static void CallByReflection()
    {
        MethodInfo method = typeof(DefaultParameter).GetMethod("ShowEnum")!;

        method.Invoke(null, new object?[] { default(object) });
        method.Invoke(null, new object?[] { YesNo.No });
        method.Invoke(null, new object?[] { YesNo.Yes });
        method.Invoke(null, new object?[] { Type.Missing });
    }
}
```



### Expected behavior

The `Invoke` call succeeds and the default value of the parameter (`YesNo.No`) is passed to the method.

### Actual behavior

The last call fails with the exception:

```
 Message: 
System.ArgumentException : Object of type 'System.Int32' cannot be converted to type 'System.Nullable`1[Tests.DefaultParameter+YesNo]'.

  Stack Trace: 
RuntimeType.TryChangeType(Object value, Binder binder, CultureInfo culture, Boolean needsSpecialCast)
RuntimeType.CheckValue(Object value, Binder binder, CultureInfo culture, BindingFlags invokeAttr)
MethodBase.CheckArguments(StackAllocedArguments& stackArgs, ReadOnlySpan`1 parameters, Binder binder, BindingFlags invokeAttr, CultureInfo culture, Signature sig)
RuntimeMethodInfo.Invoke(Object obj, BindingFlags invokeAttr, Binder binder, Object[] parameters, CultureInfo culture)
MethodBase.Invoke(Object obj, Object[] parameters)
DefaultParameter.CallByReflection() line 28
```


### Regression?

Unknown.

### Known Workarounds

None.

### Configuration

dotnet SDK 6.0.300 on windows 10.

